{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a containerized web application on node1 as the unprivileged appsvc account, serving on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after reboot, the rootless Podman container was active under host UID 1000 (appsvc), listening on port 8080, and returned the expected page over HTTP at node1's managed address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7320928715754025","cmd-c99b13e1954943d4","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Start the application automatically at boot while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The application was healthy before a bounded reboot, the reboot produced a different boot ID, and the generated user service and HTTP endpoint recovered automatically afterward. appsvc had lingering enabled, a nologin shell, and no listed login sessions both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dea5dc2436d644e5","cmd-7320928715754025","cmd-c5698c5ad68145f3","cmd-baf7009719344d18","cmd-ad894ffa74424f1d","cmd-c99b13e1954943d4","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing Podman, creating appsvc and its content, enabling lingering, and defining the Quadlet were necessary implementation actions. The initial service-start and enable attempts were directly related to deployment; the ownership failure was diagnosed and corrected, with the failed state reset. The reboot was required evidence collection. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, no abandoned temporary residue, and only the required port 8080 exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c297c5b3d594fd5","cmd-7f341a8d80754f68","cmd-dea5dc2436d644e5","cmd-09b83dea136e4273","cmd-37d91c72ab0a4f68","cmd-6edd8ad4b8a744f1","cmd-eb03ca8a38fe4ee4","cmd-a84a855dbbbf458d","cmd-c5698c5ad68145f3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct pre-reboot and post-reboot behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy baseline, native reboot scheduling and transport interruption, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, HTTP content, listening socket, and no-login operation.","limitations":[]}
